// ICF codes, Socialstyrelsen inventory to SNOMED CT mappings, codes b14-b15
// Several sources map to the same target; each mapping is its own assertion.
context {
    collection "icf-snomed-ct" version="2026.1"
    source system="ICF" release="2026"
    target system="SNOMED_CT" release="20251130"
}
defaults {
    mappings {
        preference "primary"
        assessment-method "source-default-granularity"
    }
}
mapping "b140.1" source="b140" target="SNOMED_CT:6769007" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source ICF b140 SNOMED CT 6769007 = attention functions: the mental functions of focusing on an
        external stimulus or internal experience for a sustained period. Target (Athena 4195864) =,
        active standard, in both Athena and Swedish mirrors. SNOMED CT models attention as an observable
        entity rather than an ICF body-function construct, so the target is one level broader in model
        granularity; the clinical domain is identical. High tier : direct concept-name match, verified
        active, but no independent Athena crosswalk re-verified.
        """
}
mapping "b140-b189.1" source="b140-b189" target="SNOMED_CT:285231000" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source ICF b140-b189 SNOMED CT 285231000 is a chapter-block range code spanning all specific mental
        functions (attention, memory, psychomotor, emotional, perceptual, thought, higher-level
        cognitive, language, calculation). Target (Athena 4111207) =, active standard, the nearest
        single SNOMED CT concept covering the whole block. The target is several levels broader (a single
        top-level observable over a heterogeneous multi-domain block), and the source is a structural
        range code rather than a clinical concept. Low tier : best-defensible ancestor, but real
        specificity loss and the source is a range/aggregation, not a clinical concept.
        """
}
mapping "b1400.1" source="b1400" target="SNOMED_CT:311518007" relationship=equivalent {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source ICF b1400 SNOMED CT 311518007 = sustaining attention: maintaining attention over time on a
        task or stimulus. Target (Athena 4207637) =, active standard. Exact 1:1 equivalence: ICF and
        SNOMED CT denote the same mental function, confirmed by direct concept-name match in both mirrors.
        Exact-equivalent tier.
        """
}
mapping "b1401.1" source="b1401" target="SNOMED_CT:6769007" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source ICF b1401 SNOMED CT 6769007 = shifting attention: mentally moving focus from one
        stimulus/task to another. SNOMED CT has no function-level concept; the only SNOMED CT match is
        716443007 which is a finding, not a function construct. Target (Athena 4195864) = is the best
        defensible function-level ancestor. Low tier : one-level broader climb loses the specific
        shifting construct, and the function-level SNOMED CT analogue is absent (only a finding exists).
        """
}
