mapping "b1528B.1" source="b1528B" target="SNOMED_CT:267076002" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b1528B SNOMED CT 267076002 = ICF b1528 (other specified emotional functions)
        Swedish-extension 5th-level code: the feeling of INVOLUNTARY loneliness (loneliness not
        chosen/wanted). Target (Athena 4147192) =, active standard, Swedish synonyms. The SNOMED CT concept
        is the direct named equivalent of the loneliness construct and sits under 106126000. Broader
        rather than exact (high): SNOMED CT does not encode the qualifier the ICF code carries (involuntary
        = loneliness experienced as imposed/unwanted, a valence SNOMED CT omits); the target legitimately
        subsumes the source and the qualifier gap is small and well-understood. High tier: strong
        Swedish-synonym match and verified active in both mirrors via the sctid_to_athena_id crosswalk.
        """
}
mapping "b1528C.1" source="b1528C" target="SNOMED_CT:54038000" relationship=related_to {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b1528C SNOMED CT 54038000 = ICF b1528 (other specified emotional functions)
        Swedish-extension 5th-level code: the emotional feeling of insecurity / unsafety (otrygghet =
        feeling unsafe/insecure, an affective state distinct from cognitive osäkerhet/uncertainty).
        Target (Athena 4204229) =, active standard; sits under 106126000 is an emotional-state concept.
        Related rather than broader/exact: is a generic finding whose Swedish synonym is (uncertainty) —
        it overlaps the source but does not reliably denote the affective feeling-of-unsafety the ICF
        code names, and SNOMED CT has no dedicated / concept (the concepts 159891000146105 etc. are all
        situational child-care self-efficacy Likert items). Weak tier : a defensible clinical lead (the
        only standard insecurity concept, in the emotional-state hierarchy) but with a real
        paradigm/scope gap, so recorded as a related lead not an identity, per the related-vs-no_match
        boundary rule.
        """
}
