mapping "b1564.1" source="b1564" target="SNOMED_CT:785767004" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.71 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b1564 SNOMED CT 785767004 (Tactile perception) = ICF b1564: mental functions of recognizing
        and interpreting touch stimuli (the perceptual/cortical processing of touch, as a body
        function). Target (Athena 37206160) =, active standard, Swedish synonym. The SNOMED CT concept is
        the only standard touch-perception observable and its Swedish synonym directly matches the
        source. Broader rather than exact (high): SNOMED CT is an observable (a measurable/perceptible
        characteristic) whereas ICF b1564 is explicitly a FUNCTION construct — same domain, different
        modelling paradigm, with the target fully subsuming the source's meaning. High tier: strong
        Swedish-synonym match and verified crosswalk; one-level paradigm-broader (cf. the
        function-vs-observable convention used for b1560-b1563 where a FSN exists; here no observable
        exists so 785767004 is the closest standard concept).
        """
}
mapping "b1565.1" source="b1565" target="SNOMED_CT:304653001" relationship=related_to {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b1565 SNOMED CT 304653001 (Visuospatial perception) = ICF b1565: mental functions of
        recognizing and interpreting the spatial relationships of objects and the visual field. Target
        (Athena 4121496) =, active standard. SNOMED CT has no dedicated observable (the visuospatial
        concepts are either agnosia findings 285758006, or reasoning/ability observables
        304653001/304655008/304656009, or assessment subscales). Related rather than broader/narrower:
        304653001 models visuospatial REASONING (a higher cognitive ability), whereas the source models
        visuospatial PERCEPTION (a sensory-perceptual function); these are clinically associated but not
        the same construct, neither subsumes the other cleanly (perception and reasoning are distinct
        cognitive tiers). Low tier : the only standard visuospatial observable in the cognitive
        hierarchy, with a defensible association but a real perception-vs-reasoning scope gap, per the
        related-vs-no_match boundary (association is real and defensible, so related not no_match).
        """
}
